course: dictionary
lesson: 4540
title: Heartbeat: one beat, a rhythm, a quick moment
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A heartbeat is a noun, and it can be one thing or a steady pattern. Break the word into its two parts: heart and beat. One beat is one thump of the heart as it pumps blood round the body. Your heartbeat is the steady rhythm you can feel on your wrist or neck.
explain: Read the words around a word to find its meaning. «In exercise a very fast heartbeat is normal for a healthy child.» Here heartbeat means how quickly the heart is going, and the words fast and exercise tell you it speeds up when you move. Heartbeat can also be part of a phrase: «In a heartbeat» means very quickly, without stopping to think.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If you swap in «a very fast beat of the heart is normal», the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Phrases are different from single words, so check the whole phrase, not just its parts.
fact: A heartbeat is one beat of the heart as it pumps blood.
fact: Your heartbeat is the steady sound or rhythm of your heart beating.
fact: «In a heartbeat» means very quickly, without stopping to think.
fact: To find your heartbeats per minute, count for 15 seconds and multiply by 4.
fact: Sharks can feel the weak electricity from a fish's heartbeat, even when the fish is buried in sand.
exercise: Sam counts 18 heartbeats in 15 seconds. About how many beats per minute is that? | 18 | *72 | 33
exercise: Nina says, «She would help her friend in a heartbeat.» What does «in a heartbeat» mean? | Under the water | Once a year | *Very quickly, without stopping to think | Very slowly
exercise: «Each heartbeat sends out a weak electric buzz into the water.» What does each heartbeat send out? | Light | Bubbles of air | Sand | *A weak electric buzz
test: What is a heartbeat? | *One beat of the heart as it pumps blood | The sound of a door closing | A kind of sport | A bone in the chest
test: «Chest pain or fainting is not normal and must be told to an adult.» What should you do if you have chest pain? | Ignore it because it is normal | Keep exercising harder | *Tell an adult straight away
exam: Which phrase means very quickly, without stopping to think? | Fast heartbeat | Count your heartbeat | Hospital machine | *In a heartbeat
